[ti:(untitled)]
[ar:VESAHE · hkfaduio]
[al:Sanatan & Devotional]
[by:Radio Vaigyaaniq — draft timing, unverified]
[00:08.00]भाग ३: मच्छरी का उत्तर Bhāg 3: Machcharī kā Uttar (The Mosquito's Reply)
[00:10.64]तू अपने बलकान खातिर
[00:13.28]जो एक बूँद चूस आवे से..
[00:15.92]Tū apne balkān khātir
[00:18.56]jo ek bū̃d cūs āve se..
[00:21.20]For the sake of your children
[00:23.84]that one drop I come to sip..
[00:26.48]I do not come to disturb your meditation.
[00:29.12]I do not come to test your advaita.
[00:31.76]I come because my young are hungry.
[00:34.40]I come because a river of blood
[00:37.04]is to me what the Ganga is to you—
[00:39.68]sacred, sustaining, simple.
[00:42.32]You see a mosquito.
[00:44.96]I see motherhood.
[00:47.60]You see an itch.
[00:50.24]I see survival.
[00:52.88]इसके के आग लगे से
[00:55.52]जो तन्हें दूर भगावे से..
[00:58.16]Iske ke āg lage se
[01:00.80]jo tanheṅ dūr bhagāve se..
[01:03.44]May fire consume the one
[01:06.07]who drives me away..
[01:08.71]Not a curse—
[01:11.35]a cry.
[01:13.99]When you wave your hand,
[01:16.63]you are not protecting your jñāna.
[01:19.27]You are telling a mother:
[01:21.91]Your hunger does not belong here.
[01:24.55]Your body does not belong here.
[01:27.19]Your life is a disturbance to my peace.
[01:29.83]What kind of peace
[01:32.47]is built on pushing away
[01:35.11]the small, the hungry, the other?
[01:37.75]You chant vayam sādhanā asti—
[01:40.39]We are the practice.
[01:43.03]But your we did not include me.
[01:45.67]Your sādhanā did not include
[01:48.31]the weight of my belly,
[01:50.95]the urgency of my young,
[01:53.59]the ancient rhythm of this proboscis
[01:56.23]seeking what it needs to create life.
[01:58.87]You wanted advaita—
[02:01.51]the unbroken, the still, the grand.
[02:04.15]But advaita without karuṇā (compassion)
[02:06.79]is just another name for numbness.
[02:09.43]Let me teach you now,
[02:12.07]as I taught you then:
[02:14.71]Your blood is not yours alone.
[02:17.35]It belongs to the soil, the rain, the mango tree,
[02:19.99]and to me—
[02:22.63]to my children yet to be born.
[02:25.27]When I land on your arm,
[02:27.91]I am not breaking your meditation.
[02:30.55]I am completing it.
[02:33.19]Because meditation that excludes life
[02:35.83]is not meditation.
[02:38.47]It is escape.
[02:41.11]You asked for a mantra.
[02:43.75]I give it now:
[02:46.39]Let the one who is hungry
[02:49.03]be fed by you.
[02:51.67]Let the one who is small
[02:54.31]be seen by you.
[02:56.95]Let the one who annoys you
[02:59.59]be your guru.
[03:02.22]This is vayam.
[03:04.86]This is sādhanā.
[03:07.50]This is the only anthem.
[03:10.14]I do not need your praise.
[03:12.78]I do not need your gratitude.
[03:15.42]I only need your stillness
[03:18.06]when I come.
[03:20.70]If you can give that—
[03:23.34]if you can sit with open arm
[03:25.98]and let me take what I need—
[03:28.62]then you will know:
[03:31.26]तू ही मच्छरी है
[03:33.90]तू ही पंडित है
[03:36.54]तू ही बूँद है
[03:39.18]तू ही ब्रह्म है
[03:41.82]Tū hī machcharī hai
[03:44.46]tū hī paṇḍit hai
[03:47.10]tū hī bū̃d hai
[03:49.74]tū hī brahma hai
[03:52.38]You are the mosquito
[03:55.02]You are the scholar
[03:57.66]You are the drop
[04:00.30]You are Brahman
[04:02.94]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[04:05.58]Dhīmī dhīmī hmmmmm
[04:08.22]Softly, softly… hmmmmm
[04:10.86]Not a threat.
[04:13.50]Not a curse.
[04:16.14]Just the sound of life
[04:18.78]continuing.
[04:21.42]If you hear it as mantra,
[04:24.06]you are free.
[04:26.70]If you hear it as disturbance,
[04:29.34]you are still a pandit
[04:31.98]who has not yet understood.
[04:34.62]भाग ४: आगे बढ़ायें Bhāg 4: Aage Badhāyen (Moving Forward)
[04:37.26]The Stillness
[04:39.90]अब न हाथ हिलावे
[04:42.54]अब न मन चिढ़ावे
[04:45.18]जो आए सो आए
[04:47.82]जो जाए सो जाए
[04:50.46]Ab na hāth hilāve
[04:53.10]ab na man chiṛhāve
[04:55.74]jo āe so āe
[04:58.37]jo jāe so jāe
[05:01.01]Now no hand waves away
[05:03.65]Now no mind is vexed
[05:06.29]What comes, let it come
[05:08.93]What goes, let it go
[05:11.57]The mosquito drinks. A single drop. Then another. The pandit feels the faint sting, the small weight, the brief intimacy of another life touching his own.
[05:14.21]He whispers:
[05:16.85]तेरा रक्त मेरा रक्त
[05:19.49]तेरा बच्चा मेरा बच्चा
[05:22.13]तेरी भूख मेरी भूख
[05:24.77]तेरा जीवन मेरा जीवन
[05:27.41]Terā rakta merā rakta
[05:30.05]terā baccā merā baccā
[05:32.69]terī bhūkh merī bhūkh
[05:35.33]terā jīvan merā jīvan
[05:37.97]Your blood is my blood
[05:40.61]Your child is my child
[05:43.25]Your hunger is my hunger
[05:45.89]Your life is my life
[05:48.53]The Buzzing Returns
[05:51.17]The mosquito, finished, rests on his hand. She does not buzz in question. She buzzes in affirmation—a low, steady hum, like a tanpura.
[05:53.81]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[05:56.45]अब समझ गया रे पंडित
[05:59.09]अब समझ गया
[06:01.73]Dhīmī dhīmī hmmmmm
[06:04.37]ab samajh gayā re paṇḍit
[06:07.01]ab samajh gayā
[06:09.65]Softly, softly, hmmmmm
[06:12.29]Now you understand, O pandit
[06:14.93]Now you understand
[06:17.57]The pandit opens his eyes. He looks at the mosquito on his hand. He does not see a pest. He does not see a teacher. He sees simply: life touching life.
[06:20.21]He says:
[06:22.85]तू न आई थी मुझे सिखाने
[06:25.49]मैं न बैठा था तुझे जानने
[06:28.13]फिर भी कुछ हुआ
[06:30.77]वही सत्य है
[06:33.41]Tū na āī thī mujhe sikhāne
[06:36.05]maiṅ na baiṭhā thā tujhe jānne
[06:38.69]phir bhī kuch huā
[06:41.33]vahī satya hai
[06:43.97]You did not come to teach me
[06:46.61]I did not sit to know you
[06:49.25]Yet something happened
[06:51.89]That is the truth
[06:54.52]The Anthem Merges
[06:57.16]He remembers his Quantum Anthem—the fragments, the Sanskrit, the grand declarations. Now it sounds different.
[06:59.80]He hums, softly:
[07:02.44]Q U ANT U MAN THEM
[07:05.08]q u an TUM ANT HEM
[07:07.72]He smiles.
[07:10.36]यही अंत है
[07:13.00]यही हेम है
[07:15.64]यही संगम है
[07:18.28]यही ब्रह्म है
[07:20.92]Yahī ant hai
[07:23.56]yahī hem hai
[07:26.20]yahī saṅgam hai
[07:28.84]yahī brahma hai
[07:31.48]This is the edge
[07:34.12]This is the boundary
[07:36.76]This is the confluence
[07:39.40]This is Brahman
[07:42.04]The mosquito lifts. She hovers before his face for a moment—close enough that he feels the breeze of her wings.
[07:44.68]She says—or perhaps the wind says, or perhaps his own heart says:
[07:47.32]The Final Teaching
